---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../../consts';
import '../../styles/academic-project.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`NJ Startup Signals | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="Second-place Stevens Business + AI Hackathon project mapping New Jersey startups using public funding, research, and patent signals. My work covered the backend, data pipelines, Supabase database, and API integrations." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="academic-project">
			<div class="project-header">
				<p class="project-context">Stevens Business + AI Hackathon · September 2026 · 2nd Place</p>
				<h1>NJ Startup Signals</h1>
				<p class="subtitle">An interactive platform for exploring New Jersey startups through public evidence of funding, research activity, and patents.</p>
				<p class="project-context">Team project for the 1435 Capital challenge</p>
				<ul class="technologies" aria-label="Technologies used">
					<li>TypeScript</li>
					<li>Supabase</li>
					<li>React</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class="iframe-container glass-card">
				<iframe src="https://startup-signals.vercel.app/" title="NJ Startup Signals application" loading="lazy"></iframe>
			</div>
			<div class="project-links">
				<a href="https://startup-signals.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-link">Open the App &rarr;</a>
				<a href="https://github.com/PhilPNG/StartupSignals" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-link">View Repository &rarr;</a>
				<a href="https://github.com/PhilPNG/StartupSignals/blob/main/ChallengeStatement.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-link">Read Challenge Statement &rarr;</a>
				<a href="/assets/presentations/nj-startup-signals-pitch.pptx" download class="project-link">Download Pitch Slides (.pptx) &rarr;</a>
			</div>

			<section class="prose glass-card">
				<h2>Project Overview</h2>
				<p>We built NJ Startup Signals during the Stevens Business + AI Hackathon for the 1435 Capital challenge, ultimately placing second. The app brings public signals about New Jersey companies into a map, ranked list, and sector view. Visitors can filter companies, adjust the weight of different signals, and open a company profile to inspect the underlying records and source links.</p>
			</section>

			<section class="prose glass-card">
				<h2>My Contributions</h2>
				<ul class="contributions">
					<li><strong>Built the data pipelines.</strong> I found and connected public data sources, including SEC Form D filings, research grant records from the NSF, NIH, and SBIR, and USPTO patent records. I implemented the ingestion and processing steps that turn those different sources into company and signal data for the app.</li>
					<li><strong>Set up the database.</strong> I configured the Supabase database and the data model for companies, source records, and published signals, so the app could serve traceable results rather than a static demo list.</li>
					<li><strong>Connected the APIs.</strong> I built the Next.js backend endpoints that return ranked companies, company details, sector information, and data-source status. The frontend uses those endpoints to update results when visitors change filters and signal weights.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="prose glass-card">
				<h2>How It Works</h2>
				<ol class="pipeline">
					<li><strong>Collect public records.</strong> The backend pipeline imports available funding, grant, and patent data from the external sources.</li>
					<li><strong>Link records to companies.</strong> Source records are processed and stored in Supabase with their provenance, then organized into signals for each company.</li>
					<li><strong>Serve interactive results.</strong> The API scores and ranks companies using the visitor’s selected signal weights. The frontend presents the results on a map and in a list, sorted by score and visualized by sector.</li>
				</ol>
				<p>Source coverage varies by company. The app separates live results from clearly labeled sample data, and its AI-generated summaries are a separate part of the team’s work.</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.iframe-container {
		width: 100%;
		height: 75vh;
		min-height: 620px;
		padding: 0;
		overflow: hidden;
	}
	iframe {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		border: 0;
	}
	.project-links {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.75em;
		margin-top: 1.5em;
		margin-bottom: 2em;
	}
	.project-links .project-link {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.contributions {
		padding-left: 1.5em;
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}
	.contributions li + li {
		margin-top: 1em;
	}
	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.iframe-container {
			height: 70vh;
			min-height: 500px;
		}
	}
</style>
